---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
	{ label: 'Home', href: '/' },
	{ label: 'Methodology & Disclaimer' },
];
---

<Layout
	title="Methodology & US FLSA Disclaimer | NetHourly"
	description="How NetHourly calculates gross pay, 26 bi-weekly pay periods, FLSA overtime, 24-hour shift sleep and meal deductions, and estimated US take-home pay."
>
	<Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="mesh" aria-hidden="true"></div>
		<div class="shell hero-inner">
			<p class="eyebrow mono">Methodology · US payroll · FLSA</p>
			<h1>How NetHourly calculates pay.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Every figure on NetHourly comes from the same US payroll conventions: a 52-week year,
				FLSA overtime after 40 hours, 26 bi-weekly pay periods, and clearly labeled tax
				estimates. Here is exactly what each number means.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="content">
		<div class="shell content-grid">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Why NetHourly exists</h2>
				<p>
					Most workers do not need another finance blog. They need to know what a $22/hour
					offer means on a bi-weekly check, why a 24-hour shift paid 13 hours instead of 24,
					or why a big overtime check looked heavily taxed. Those questions have concrete
					answers, and the answers should be visible.
				</p>
				<p>
					NetHourly is an independent calculator and reference site for US hourly and shift
					workers. The goal is to make the math legible: show the formula, label the
					assumptions, and separate gross pay from take-home estimates. The site does not
					collect payroll data and does not replace a payroll department, a tax preparer, or a
					lawyer.
				</p>

				<h2>1. Gross pay and pay periods</h2>
				<p>
					Gross pay is pay before any tax withholding or deductions. For an hourly worker, the
					baseline is 40 hours per week for 52 weeks, or 2,080 hours per year. Weekly gross is
					the hourly rate × 40. Annual gross is weekly gross × 52.
				</p>
				<div class="formula">Annual gross = hourly rate × 40 hours × 52 weeks</div>
				<p>
					Pay frequency changes the size of each paycheck, not the annual total:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Weekly:</strong> annual gross ÷ 52 paychecks.</li>
					<li><strong>Bi-weekly:</strong> annual gross ÷ 26 paychecks — the most common US schedule.</li>
					<li><strong>Semi-monthly:</strong> annual gross ÷ 24 paychecks, usually paid on the 1st and 15th.</li>
					<li><strong>Monthly:</strong> annual gross ÷ 12 paychecks.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Bi-weekly and semi-monthly are not interchangeable. Twenty-six bi-weekly checks are
					smaller than twenty-four semi-monthly checks, even though annual gross is identical.
				</p>

				<h2>2. FLSA overtime</h2>
				<p>
					Under the federal Fair Labor Standards Act, most non-exempt employees earn 1.5× their
					regular rate for hours worked beyond 40 in a fixed 7-day workweek. Double time is 2×
					and is not required by federal law, but may apply under state law, a union contract, or
					employer policy.
				</p>
				<div class="formula">Overtime pay = overtime hours × hourly rate × 1.5</div>
				<div class="formula">Double-time pay = double-time hours × hourly rate × 2</div>
				<p>
					Some states add daily overtime. California, for example, pays 1.5× after 8 hours in a
					workday and 2× after 12 hours. The 24-hour shift calculator supports both the federal
					weekly method and the California daily split.
				</p>

				<h2>3. 24-hour shifts, sleep, and meals</h2>
				<p>
					A 24-hour shift is not automatically 24 paid hours. FLSA rules allow employers to
					exclude up to 8 hours of sleep time only when the worker receives at least 5 hours of
					uninterrupted sleep. Up to 3 duty-free meal hours — typically one hour each for
					breakfast, lunch, and dinner — may also be excluded.
				</p>
				<div class="formula">Payable hours = 24 − sleep deduction − meal deduction</div>
				<p>
					With the full 8 sleep hours and 3 meal hours excluded, 13 of the 24 hours remain
					payable. If the worker must remain on duty, or sleep is interrupted below the 5-hour
					threshold, the time is generally compensable. Actual arrangements depend on the
					employment relationship and applicable state rules.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Estimated take-home pay</h2>
				<p>
					NetHourly does not prepare tax returns. The take-home toggle applies simplified,
					flat-rate estimates to gross pay:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>FICA only:</strong> 7.65% — 6.2% Social Security plus 1.45% Medicare.</li>
					<li><strong>Standard single filer:</strong> about 18% — FICA plus roughly 10.35% effective federal income tax.</li>
					<li><strong>High-tax state:</strong> about 24% — adds state income tax for places such as California, New York, New Jersey, and Oregon.</li>
					<li><strong>No-income-tax state:</strong> about 15% — FICA plus federal tax only, for places such as Texas, Florida, Washington, and Nevada.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Real withholding depends on filing status, dependents, pre-tax deductions, credits,
					and state or local rules. Use the estimates to compare scenarios, not to calculate an
					exact paycheck.
				</p>

				<h2>5. Sources and further reading</h2>
				<p>
					These are the primary references behind the calculators. Rules change; check the
					current version before relying on a figure.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd" rel="noopener noreferrer">
							US Department of Labor, Wage and Hour Division
						</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a
							href="https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/fact-sheets/23-flsa-overtime-pay"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							DOL Fact Sheet #23: Overtime Pay
						</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a
							href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-29/subtitle-B/chapter-V/subchapter-A/part-785/subpart-C/section-785.22"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							29 CFR § 785.22: Sleep time
						</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.dir.ca.gov/dlse/faq_overtime.htm" rel="noopener noreferrer">
							California DIR: Overtime FAQ
						</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.irs.gov/publications/p15" rel="noopener noreferrer">
							IRS Publication 15: Employer's Tax Guide
						</a>
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>6. Methodology &amp; US FLSA disclaimer</h2>

				<p>
					NetHourly is an independent educational calculator. It is not a payroll provider, law
					firm, or tax adviser, and it is not affiliated with the US Department of Labor or any
					state agency. Wage and hour law is fact-specific and changes over time. Overtime
					eligibility, sleep and meal exclusions, and state daily overtime rules depend on the
					worker's duties, employment agreement, and location.
				</p>
				<p>
					Always confirm current rules with the US Department of Labor, your state labor office,
					or a qualified payroll or legal professional before relying on a figure for a
					paycheck, contract, or dispute.
				</p>
			</div>

			<aside class="summary-card" aria-label="Calculation summary">
				<span class="mono">At a glance</span>
				<div class="summary-row">
					<span>Full-time baseline</span>
					<code>40 hrs × 52 weeks</code>
				</div>
				<div class="summary-row">
					<span>Annual gross</span>
					<code>rate × 2,080</code>
				</div>
				<div class="summary-row">
					<span>Bi-weekly</span>
					<code>annual ÷ 26</code>
				</div>
				<div class="summary-row">
					<span>Semi-monthly</span>
					<code>annual ÷ 24</code>
				</div>
				<div class="summary-row">
					<span>FLSA overtime</span>
					<code>rate × 1.5 after 40</code>
				</div>
				<div class="summary-row">
					<span>FICA</span>
					<code>7.65% of gross</code>
				</div>
				<div class="summary-row">
					<span>Standard estimate</span>
					<code>~18% total</code>
				</div>
				<a class="button button-primary" href="/#calculator-band">Run your numbers</a>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page-hero {
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
		padding: 72px 0 48px;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.mesh {
		position: absolute;
		inset: -280px -10% auto;
		height: 640px;
		background:
			radial-gradient(38% 55% at 18% 42%, rgba(0, 124, 240, 0.28), transparent 70%),
			radial-gradient(32% 50% at 44% 20%, rgba(121, 40, 202, 0.22), transparent 72%),
			radial-gradient(38% 55% at 70% 44%, rgba(255, 0, 128, 0.15), transparent 72%),
			radial-gradient(30% 48% at 88% 22%, rgba(249, 203, 40, 0.2), transparent 72%);
		filter: blur(36px);
		pointer-events: none;
		-webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 40%, transparent 100%);
		mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 40%, transparent 100%);
	}

	.hero-inner {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.hero-inner .eyebrow {
		color: var(--mute);
	}

	h1 {
		max-width: 860px;
		margin: 20px 0 0;
		font-size: clamp(38px, 6.4vw, 62px);
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1;
		letter-spacing: -2.8px;
	}

	.lede {
		max-width: 700px;
		margin: 18px 0 0;
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 27px;
		color: var(--body);
	}

	.content {
		padding: 64px 0 96px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
	}

	.content-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 320px;
		gap: 64px;
		align-items: start;
	}

	.prose {
		max-width: 720px;
	}

	.prose h2 {
		margin: 40px 0 0;
		font-size: clamp(24px, 3.2vw, 32px);
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1.15;
		letter-spacing: -1.2px;
	}

	.prose h2:first-child {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.prose p {
		margin: 12px 0 0;
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 26px;
		color: var(--body);
	}

	.prose ul {
		margin: 14px 0 0;
		padding: 0 0 0 20px;
	}

	.prose li {
		margin: 8px 0 0;
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 25px;
		color: var(--body);
	}

	.prose strong {
		color: var(--ink);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.formula {
		margin: 14px 0 0;
		padding: 10px 12px;
		border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--canvas-elevated);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 12px;
		line-height: 18px;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.summary-card {
		position: sticky;
		top: 96px;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 12px;
		padding: 20px;
		border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
		border-radius: 12px;
		background: var(--canvas-elevated);
	}

	.summary-card > .mono {
		color: var(--mute);
	}

	.summary-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 4px;
		padding-top: 12px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
	}

	.summary-row span {
		font-size: 12px;
		color: var(--mute);
	}

	.summary-row code {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 12px;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.summary-card .button {
		margin-top: 8px;
	}

	@media (max-width: 960px) {
		.content-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 32px;
		}

		.summary-card {
			position: static;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.page-hero {
			padding: 52px 0 36px;
		}

		h1 {
			letter-spacing: -2px;
		}

		.lede {
			font-size: 15px;
			line-height: 24px;
		}

		.content {
			padding: 48px 0 72px;
		}
	}
</style>
